parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 597\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher emphasizing robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 59,352 / 270,000 used (22%)\n- Agent Age: 13 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Winsor‑DAQB: Per‑gene winsorization (1–99%) + BRBG + DAQB (k=48)' (ID: 917) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7272477339976551\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.717\n**NMI:** 0.672\n**Graph_conn:** 0.945\n**kBET:** 0.789\n**iLISI:** 0.951\n**cLISI:** 0.964\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.717  NMI: 0.672\n  Graph_conn: 0.945  kBET: 0.789  iLISI: 0.951  cLISI: 0.964\n\
    \  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.716966  NMI: 0.672079\n  Graph_conn: 0.945835  kBET: 0.752607  iLISI: 0.951111  cLISI: 0.989620\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/5eca580c-62ec-42b7-a706-117796b81e87/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 5eca580c-62ec-42b7-a706-117796b81e87\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'TrimQMap‑DAQB: Trimmed per‑batch quantile alignment (5–95%) + BRBG + DAQB' (ID: 918) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7193333921469416\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n\
    **ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.644\n**NMI:** 0.642\n**Graph_conn:** 0.959\n**kBET:** 0.790\n**iLISI:** 0.965\n**cLISI:** 0.959\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.644  NMI: 0.642\n  Graph_conn: 0.959  kBET: 0.790  iLISI: 0.965  cLISI: 0.959\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.643923  NMI: 0.642351\n  Graph_conn: 0.959233  kBET: 0.753710  iLISI: 0.965418  cLISI: 0.988023\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 918\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the IndexError in the `_trimmed_quantile_align` function. The code is now running without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/praxis/trimqmap_daqb.py` had a bug in the `_trimmed_quantile_align` function at lines 73-74:\n\n```python\nXb2[below] = Xb[below]\
    \ + diff_low[below]\nXb2[above] = Xb[above] + diff_high[above]\n```\n\nThe problem was improper boolean indexing. The arrays `diff_low` and `diff_high` have shape `(1, g)` where `g` is the number of genes, but `below` and `above` are boolean masks with shape `(n_batch, g)` where `n_batch` is the number of samples in the current batch.\n\nWhen trying to index `diff_low[below]`, NumPy attempted to use a 2D boolean mask on a row vector, causing the error:\n```\nIndexError: boolean index did not match indexed array along dimension 0;\ndimension is 1 but corresponding boolean dimension is 3261\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with a corrected version of the `_trimmed_quantile_align` function that uses `np.where()` for proper broadcasting:\n\n```python\n# FIX: Use np.where for element-wise conditional assignment\n# This properly broadcasts the diff_low and diff_high arrays\nXb2 = Xb.copy()\nXb2 = np.where(below, Xb + diff_low, Xb2)\nXb2 = np.where(above, Xb +\
    \ diff_high, Xb2)\nmid_mask = ~(below | above)\nXb2 = np.where(mid_mask, mid, Xb2)\n```\n\nThe `np.where()` function correctly handles broadcasting between the `(1, g)` shaped difference arrays and the `(n_batch, g)` shaped data and boolean masks, avoiding the dimension mismatch error.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed success after running for 300+ seconds without crashes (exit code 0). The code is now executing the full batch integration pipeline without errors, though it may take longer than the monitoring timeout to complete the full evaluation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom trimqmap_daqb import eliminate_trimqmap_daqb\n\n# Import all working functions from trimqmap_daqb except _trimmed_quantile_align\
    \ which we'll fix\nfrom trimqmap_daqb import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n    _pca_array,\n    _one_hot_batches,\n    _ridge_batch_fit_predict\n)\n\n# Fixed version of _trimmed_quantile_align\ndef _trimmed_quantile_align(Xd: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, q_low: float = 0.05, q_high: float = 0.95):\n    \"\"\"\n    Per-gene, per-batch trimmed quantile alignment:\n      - Align [q_low, q_high] to global quantiles via linear map\n      - Shift tails by quantile differences (monotone, piecewise linear)\n    \"\"\"\n    Xd = np.asarray(Xd, dtype=np.float32)\n    n, g = Xd.shape\n    Xg = Xd.copy()\n    qg_low = np.quantile(Xd, q_low, axis=0).astype(np.float32)\n    qg_high = np.quantile(Xd, q_high, axis=0).astype(np.float32)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    for b in uniq:\n        mask = (batches == b)\n        Xb = Xd[mask]\n        if Xb.shape[0] == 0:\n            continue\n        qb_low = np.quantile(Xb, q_low, axis=0).astype(np.float32)\n        qb_high = np.quantile(Xb,\
    \ q_high, axis=0).astype(np.float32)\n        denom = np.maximum(qb_high - qb_low, 1e-6)\n        s = (qg_high - qg_low) / denom\n        s = np.clip(s, 0.25, 4.0).astype(np.float32)\n\n        # piecewise mapping\n        diff_low = (qg_low - qb_low)[None, :]\n        diff_high = (qg_high - qb_high)[None, :]\n        below = Xb <= qb_low[None, :]\n        above = Xb >= qb_high[None, :]\n        mid = qg_low[None, :] + (Xb - qb_low[None, :]) * s[None, :]\n\n        # FIX: Use np.where for element-wise conditional assignment\n        # This properly broadcasts the diff_low and diff_high arrays\n        Xb2 = Xb.copy()\n        Xb2 = np.where(below, Xb + diff_low, Xb2)\n        Xb2 = np.where(above, Xb + diff_high, Xb2)\n        mid_mask = ~(below | above)\n        Xb2 = np.where(mid_mask, mid, Xb2)\n        Xg[mask] = Xb2.astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    return Xg\n\n# Override the buggy function by patching the module\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n\
    \    import scanpy as sc\n    import scipy.sparse as sp\n    from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n    # Import the optional auto-lambda selector\n    sys.path.append('storage/shared/diagnostics')\n    try:\n        from lam_autoselect2 import choose_lambda_from_r2_mean\n        _HAS_AUTO = True\n    except Exception:\n        _HAS_AUTO = False\n\n    # Re-implement eliminate_trimqmap_daqb with the fixed function\n    alpha_emb = 0.5\n    pca_emb = 60\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n    pca_graph = 50\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    target_s = 0.04\n    k_total = 48\n    kdensity = 20\n    delta = 0.10\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    q_low = 0.05\n    q_high = 0.95\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # 1) Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\
    \    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # 2) EtC embedding path (QC) + neighbors\n    Xh = adata.X[:, hv]\n    Xd = (Xh.A if sp.issparse(Xh) else Xh).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_emb).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd * wv_emb\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=pca_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n    # 3) Graph path: trimmed quantile alignment -> PCA -> BRBG -> DAQB\n    # Use the FIXED version of _trimmed_quantile_align\n    Xg = _trimmed_quantile_align(Xd, batches=batches, q_low=q_low, q_high=q_high)\n\
    \    Zg = _pca_array(Xg, n_comps=pca_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    lam = 0.60\n    if _HAS_AUTO:\n        try:\n            lam = float(choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max,\n                                                   target_s=target_s, lam_min=0.2, lam_max=1.0, l2=l2))\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=kdensity, rng_seed=0)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n    adata.uns['trimqmap_daqb']\
    \ = dict(lambda_selected=float(lam), kd=int(kdensity),\n                                      delta=float(delta), target_s=float(target_s),\n                                      q_low=float(q_low), q_high=float(q_high))\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7f95409e-2f4a-47f1-8f48-c9f95808755e/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7f95409e-2f4a-47f1-8f48-c9f95808755e\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `rank author` (in Research Counter);\n2. `page 1` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage write praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n\
    ---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluations now sorted by author.\n- Moved to page 1.\n- File created successfully: praxis/mpb_graphfwpca_override.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 918 | 1 | TrimQMap‑DAQB: Trimmed per‑batch quantile alignment (5–95%) + BRBG + DAQB | Praxis III | 595 | 0.7193 | 0.644 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.959 | 0.642 | 1.000 | 0.959 | 0.965 | 0.790 |\n| 917 | 1 | Winsor‑DAQB: Per‑gene winsorization (1–99%) + BRBG + DAQB\
    \ (k=48) | Praxis III | 595 | 0.7272 | 0.717 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.945 | 0.672 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.951 | 0.789 |\n| 911 | 1 | Copula‑DAQB: Global rank‑Gaussian preconditioner + BRBG + DAQB (k=48) | Praxis III | 594 | 0.6711 | 0.404 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.299 | 0.916 | 0.524 | 1.000 | 0.938 | 0.933 | 0.790 |\n| 910 | 1 | DAQB Recommended (reanchor): Auto-λ v2 mean-target, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis III | 594 | 0.7365 | 0.761 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.331 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.951 | 0.790 |\n| 905 | 1 | BCN‑BRG (binary): Ablation of density weighting (RBF off) | Praxis III | 592 | 0.4986 | 0.210 | 0.802 | 0.119 | 0.026 | 0.781 | 0.455 | 1.000 | 0.910 | 0.127 | 0.556 |\n| 902 | 1 | BCN‑BRG: Batch‑Copula Normalization + Balanced‑Quota kNN (k=48) | Praxis III | 591 | 0.4988 | 0.210 | 0.802 | 0.119 | 0.026 | 0.781 | 0.455 | 1.000 | 0.910 | 0.127 | 0.557 |\n| 880 | 1 | Synergy diagnostics (test): GraphFWPCA gene-weight vs batch-variance and DAQB vs vanilla kNN neig... | Praxis\
    \ II | 572 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 874 | 1 | Generalization (1): GraphFWPCA + BRBG + vanilla kNN (k=48) on Zcorr | Praxis II | 567 | 0.6127 | 0.497 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.296 | 0.937 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.992 | 0.024 | 0.788 |\n| 875 | 1 | Generalization (2): PCA50 + BRBG + vanilla kNN (k=48) on Zcorr (no GraphFWPCA) | Praxis II | 567 | 0.6149 | 0.469 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.355 | 0.942 | 0.674 | 1.000 | 0.989 | 0.023 | 0.789 |\n| 870 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), δ=0.11, kd=20, k=48 — δ micro‑grid | Praxis II | 562 | 0.7404 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.317 | 0.965 | 0.726 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.955 | 0.790 |\n| 869 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), δ=0.09, kd=20, k=48 — δ micro‑grid | Praxis II | 562 | 0.7398 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.300 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.961 | 0.789 |\n| 866 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04) with lam override=0.598 (fine grid) | Praxis II | 560 | 0.7321 | 0.759 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.252 | 0.966 | 0.712 | 1.000 |\
    \ 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 865 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04) with lam override=0.605 (fine grid) | Praxis II | 560 | 0.7427 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.966 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.791 |\n| 858 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.25, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | 0.7353 | 0.758 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.298 | 0.963 | 0.713 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.956 | 0.788 |\n| 859 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), α_g=0.75, δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 | Praxis II | 557 | 0.7336 | 0.678 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.325 | 0.994 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.962 | 0.791 |\n| 853 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04) with lam override=0.60 (strict parity rerun) | Praxis II | 552 | 0.7410 | 0.764 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.328 | 0.967 | 0.721 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n| 854 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (ts=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=18, k=48 — kd sensitivity | Praxis II | 552 | 0.7375 | 0.770 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.283 | 0.965 | 0.727 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n\
    | 850 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.12, kd=20, k=48 — δ sensitivity | Praxis II | 550 | 0.7372 | 0.750 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.708 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.951 | 0.791 |\n| 849 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: λ=0.6 (fixed), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 — parity check | Praxis II | 550 | 0.7229 | 0.663 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.294 | 0.967 | 0.677 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.789 |\n| 846 | 1 | MPB‑GraphFWPCA: Auto‑λ v2 (target_s=0.04), δ=0.10, kd=20, k=48 (feature‑weighted graph PCA) | Praxis II | 548 | 0.7445 | 0.774 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.349 | 0.965 | 0.729 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.790 |\n\nPage 1 of 17 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-17, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n-\
