  \ runs 940 and 941, I can start an ablation with δ=0.11 to test the effects.**Planning submissions and actions**\n\nWe can't submit new tasks right now due to concurrency issues, but I can prepare the submission script. I want to test kdensity with parameters 18 and 20 since earlier results with kd=18 showed promise. I should also consider a \"harmonic\" synergy aggregator, although we haven't implemented it yet. \n\nNow, while waiting for runs 940 and 941, I could return to the Reflection Chamber or write a research log summarizing insights. I can execute actions like reviewing log 938 and writing to storage with summarizing content. I need to keep comments minimal while streamlining my plans.**Composing the research log**\n\nI’m setting up the content for a research log titled \"Addendum: SoftPower γ and MPB override results (Ticks 595-605).\" In my observations, I noticed that Copula preconditioners degrade slightly, while winsor and trim quantile show small improvements. It looks like\
  \ SoftPower is surpassing the baseline with an override value of λ=0.605 and δ=0.10 yielding 0.7424. \n\nFor upcoming experiments, I plan to tune the auto-lambda mean target between 0.036 and 0.042, test δ micro-grid in the range of 0.09 to 0.12, and compare kdensity settings. I’ll also specify neighbors metric effects by using cosine versus Euclidean. I need to record this in storage, so I'll execute the necessary commands using YAML formatting to produce a clear log."
