  I need to craft the final answer with actions to continue our experiments. This interactive environment requires careful inclusion of proper coding and quoting in the /execute_action lines and YAML blocks. We achieved a state-of-the-art score of 0.7465 with a specific configuration. Looking at the leaderboard, we’re performing well! Our next steps will involve tuning and testing certain parameters, while also ensuring that our logs are updated accordingly. Let''s keep pushing forward!**Analyzing experiment performance**


  I see that experiments 963 and 964 were running at the previous ticks, but now at tick 618, they are still showing as running. The results indicate that 960 is the top performer, while experiment 961 with seed 1 regressed. It’s crucial to consider cap adjustments in the DAQB builder, but I need to verify if the cap parameter in the mpb_graphfwpca_override function was exposed properly. I''ll check earlier code references to ensure everything aligns correctly.**Reviewing code parameters**


  I need to review earlier code in the mpb_graphfwpca_override.py file. It seems I didn''t include the cap parameter, even though it has multiple other arguments like alpha_emb, delta, and rng_seed. The function build_density_adaptive_bbsg, which I called, didn’t have cap either. So if I want to include the cap, I''ll need to modify the mpb_graphfwpca_override.py file to accept it and pass it along properly. I should also check if the bbsg_density_adaptive function supports the cap argument at all. Let''s investigate further!**Preparing for updates**


  I found that the file ''bbsg_density_adaptive.py'' in the praxis directory likely accepts a cap parameter, which isn''t listed in the earlier imports. I can update mpb_graphfwpca_override.py to pass the cap argument, and I''ll create new wrappers for cap values of 1.9 and 2.2 with the best configuration. There''s also a chance to test the rng_seed at 2 with k=50, although it may have minimal effects. However, I can''t publish yet since the archive room isn''t available until after 50 ticks, so I''ll prepare documentation and adjust the meta prompt accordingly.**Planning submission actions**


  I need to propose two new submissions for my experiments, specifically for cap values of 1.9 and 2.2. However, I realize we have a limit on concurrent evaluations, so we need to wait for experiments 963 and 964 to finish before submitting anything new.


  While waiting, I can focus on writing the necessary code wrappers for cap adjustments. I also want to make sure to update the mpb_graphfwpca_override.py file to accept the cap parameter and adjust the documentation accordingly. I''ll ensure I''m prepared to submit once those experiments are complete, and also update the meta prompt with the new best scores!'
