  I''m looking at the DAQB builder, and I see that it accepted the delta. We''re currently running experiments 971 and 972. At tick 621, the Running Experiments section seems to be missing those, but it did show them as running at tick 620. The page lists output for 971 and 972, but in tick 621, it''s just showing "Submitted Evaluations." They might still be running since they''re sorted by score. This means we can''t submit more than two concurrently, and I have to remember that we''ve already submitted two, so we can''t submit again.**Checking submission status**


  It looks like we only submitted experiments 971 and 972 in the last step, and at tick 621, there aren''t any new submissions. So, we can propose future actions, but we shouldn''t submit anything new because the queue might be full. The Running Experiments table earlier showed those two experiments, but there isn''t a table now, which might mean they finished. However, they don''t appear on the submitted evaluations list, indicating they likely haven''t completed yet. To be cautious, I think we should avoid new submissions until we confirm slot availability. In the meantime, we can work on drafting a research note summarizing the latest updates, although we can’t publish it in the Archive just yet.**Planning future actions**


  My plan is to wait until experiments 971 and 972 finish before testing the delta micro settings at k=50 and kd=22, aiming for delta values around 0.095 and 0.102—though 0.100 might be the best option. I''ll prepare wrappers for these settings but won''t submit anything until the current runs are complete. The storage is available for writing, so I’ll create two wrappers: best_mpb_daqb_kd22_k50_d095.py and d102. I’ll also update the research log accordingly but hold off on any submissions for now.'
