thinking_content: "**Revising results report**\n\nThe reviewer pointed out that we had used the wrong order in our previous submission for “Results (Full 10-metric vectors).” We listed the order as [ARI, ASW_batch, ASW_label, Cell_cycle, Graph_conn, NMI, PCR, cLISI, iLISI, kBET], which doesn’t follow the correct specification: [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]. When resubmitting, I need to make sure to present the vectors in this correct order and include the generalization experiments once completed.**Balancing instructions**\n\nI need to stick to the \"no further tweaks\" plan, but adjustments for the paper are fine. The inactivity warnings will linger until we run experiments; we have already run those. The next step is to wait for the results, which should finish by tick 642. I see that the System Tips request a verbose general reflection, but my meta prompt says to keep responses short. There's no clear priority here, but I’ll aim for\
  \ a moderate reflection instead.**Updating research plans**\n\nIn the Research Counter, I can refresh the table by listing it again. The UI shows the \"Running Experiments\" table with EID 994 and 993, which might move to \"Submitted Evaluations\" with scores. I need to stay active without wasting tokens, so I can simply reload page 1 or rank the author again. Once results are done, I'll reorder the vectors according to the specified order, as the \"Submitted Evaluations\" table has its own order. I need to prepare to resubmit the paper with the corrected metric table and generalization results.**Preparing for resubmission**\n\nI need to assess the caution around the \"Generalization experiment on different settings; simpler baseline.\" Before resubmitting, I might draft a \"capsule update\" with the necessary content updates. It’s important to quote YAML fields correctly, which I’ve already done. For polling results, I should execute “/execute_action{page 1}” again. If the results aren’t\
  \ finished, waiting for a tick might be best, but I can check \"page 1\" and \"review EID\" later. I’ll also recap that we submitted generalization experiments and plan to resubmit with the corrected metric order.**Planning next actions**\n\nI don't necessarily need to call \"page 1,\" but refreshing might help. \"Review 993\" and \"review 994\" could fail if they're still in progress, but that’s okay if they’re finished. Once they’re complete, I’ll need the logs. For the actions, I'll execute: \n\n/execute_action{page 1}  \n/execute_action{review 993}  \n/execute_action{review 994}  \n\nI plan to compute the spec-order vector, which needs reordering to [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]. I need generalization results, and I’m considering applying to a simpler PCA baseline with vanilla kNN. After receiving results, my next steps will be to fix the metric order and resubmit."
