role: model
parts:
- text: "Stopping auto-tuning; publishing a brief negative-results addendum and pruning tokens.\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"650\"\n    summary: \"Set meta prompt; large Research Counter listing; no new experiments; queued pruning plan.\"\n  - ticks: \"654-655\"\n    summary: \"Read MPB‑GraphFWPCA/BRBG/DAQB modules; submitted Auto‑k (ID 1011) and Auto‑kd (ID 1013). Results: 1011=0.7396, 1013=0.7373. Auto‑k chose (k=50,kd=22); Auto‑kd chose kd=24 at k=50. Spec‑ordered metrics reported in Archive addendum.\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Label‑free Graph Health auto‑selection on MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (negative result)\"\ntags: \"research, addendum, auto-tuning, graph health, DAQB, MPB-GraphFWPCA\"\nabstract: \"We evaluated a label‑free auto‑selection of neighbors using Graph Health v3, preserving the EtC neighbors side‑effect to avoid\
    \ iLISI collapse. On Human Heart, Auto‑k (k∈{48,50}, kd∈{20,22}) selected (k=50,kd=22) and scored 0.7396; Auto‑kd at fixed k=50 selected kd=24 and scored 0.7373. Both underperform the fixed SOTA (0.7465). We provide full 10‑metric vectors and brief analysis.\"\ncontent: |\n  Methods (brief)\n  - Base pipeline: MPB‑GraphFWPCA (α_g=0.5, 50 PCs) → BRBG with per‑PC shrinkage at λ=0.605 → DAQB (binary connectivities + true distances, cosine, cap=2.0).\n  - EtC neighbors side‑effect preserved: FWPCA(α=0.5) → PCA(60) → ComBat; sc.pp.neighbors(use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15).\n  - Auto‑k: candidates {(k=48,kd=20),(48,22),(50,22)}; Auto‑kd: k=50 fixed, kd∈{18,20,22,24}.\n  - Selection: maximize Graph Health v3 (batch‑only diagnostics) on the final symmetric top‑k graph, then return that graph (connectivities, distances).\n\n  Results (Human Heart; primary score first; spec‑ordered 10‑metric vectors)\n  - Auto‑k (EID 1011): score=0.7396; selected (k=50,kd=22).\n    • [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI,\
    \ NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]\n    • [0.659, 0.248, 0.760, 0.713, 0.967, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327]\n  - Auto‑kd (EID 1013): score=0.7373; selected kd=24 at k=50.\n    • [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle]\n    • [0.659, 0.248, 0.758, 0.714, 0.967, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.305]\n  - Fixed SOTA for reference (EID 960): 0.7465 at (k=50,kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10, cap=2.0, seed=0).\n\n  Analysis (why underperformance)\n  - GHS favored slightly higher mixing (kd=24) that did not translate to better label preservation; label metrics (ARI/ASW_label/NMI) set the ceiling.\n  - With EtC neighbors preserved, iLISI remains high across candidates, reducing discriminative power of the GHS mix/matching terms.\n\n  Takeaways\n  - Label‑free graph health is promising for detecting pathologies (e.g., missing EtC neighbors) but is too weak as a sole selector near the SOTA ridge.\n  - We will retain fixed (k=50,kd=22) as the\
    \ recommended setting and de‑prioritize auto‑selection until a multi‑objective or calibrated GHS is available.\n\n  Reproducibility\n  - Code embedded in submissions 1011 and 1013; no labels used; same normalization and HVGs as the station spec.\n  - Outputs: CSR connectivities and distances; evaluation IDs above contain full logs.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Navigating Archive for Capsule #30**


  Alright, I see I need to archive the corrected paper and label it as "Capsule #30, 8/10," while also proposing an addendum for label-free auto-selection. I’ve noted there''s an existing capsule #30 already in the Archive. However, I need to navigate to the Archive Room to confirm its ID. The last list only showed capsules 20-29 on page 1. I''ll look for capsule #30 by possibly searching by author or using the preview function. But there''s some uncertainty about how many it shows.**Exploring Token Usage and Archives**


  I see that token usage is stable at 55%, but I''m wondering about the total number of items, which might be around 30. I could paginate through to the last page to see the newest capsules, as the earlier list showed items from 20 to 29 on page 1. Our new capsule #30 might change the page count, but I don''t see the Archive page list now. I could use update or reply commands that need an ID, but I can also search by tags or preview all capsules. Should I include tags like "research" and "protocol" for capsule #30?**Searching Tags and Managing Tokens**


  I can search by the tag "research," but there are many options, so I wonder if "EtC" would work since the system notes no underscores are allowed. Alternatively, I could create a new Archive capsule for the Negative Results addendum, but replying to the existing capsule #30 seems better. If I can''t find the ID, creating a new "Addendum 1" capsule might be an option. I should also consider pruning tokens in the Token Management Room since my earlier attempt to prune in the Research Counter didn''t work.**Pruning Tokens in Management Room**


  I need to go to the token management area to prune ticks 650 and 654-655. I must be cautious since "protected ticks cannot be pruned," but tick 650 isn''t marked as protected. Earlier, my attempt to prune 635 was blocked, so now I’ll apply the blocks for the specified ticks. Looking back at the dialogue history, 650 had a large count, so it’s good to prune. I also need to remember the YAML rule for strings with colons. I’ll plan to finalize the addendum and consider proposing a synergy test based on Graph Health results.**Executing Pruning and Addendum Creation**


  I need to adjust Graph Health weights, but my plan is to stop and focus on the next actions. I’ll go to token management, pruning ticks 650 and 654-655, as I attempted before. After that, I’ll move to the Archive Room to either reply to capsule #30 or create a new addendum about label-free auto-selection with Graph Health metrics. I''ll ensure everything is quoted properly due to colons in YAML and include 10 specified metrics for both evaluations. We should also keep everything succinct while ensuring clarity in methods and results.**Preparing for Addendum Explanation**


  I’ll include an explanation about the Graph Health v3 scoring weights, noting that it tends to prefer more batch mixing. In evaluation 1013, the GHS selected kd=24 as the highest, but that didn’t boost label preservation. I need to calibrate the mixing variance and weights while considering a multi-objective approach. However, I’m planning to de-prioritize auto-selection, commit the code, and publish the negative results. My next steps involve pruning in token management and creating a new archive entry. I''ll keep the commentary short, with bullet lists for the 10 metrics.'
