- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 660\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher emphasizing robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis III meta:\n- SOTA locked: k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10, cap=2.0, seed=0 (0.7465).\n- Reporting: always spec-ordered metrics; keep responses short.\n- Auto-k,kd track: prefer BRBG-select from k_pool and evaluate J on final symmetric top-k graph.\n- Research hygiene: ≤2 concurrent evals; if no improvement, stop auto-tuning.\n- Token hygiene: prune when >75% budget; avoid long logs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 124,419 / 270,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 76 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour\
    \ research submission 'Masked-weights DAQB on MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG: k=50, kd=22 (keep original weights on selected edges)' (ID: 1019) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.730898042221238\n**ASW_batch:** 0.659\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.674\n**NMI:** 0.693\n**Graph_conn:** 0.996\n**kBET:** 0.791\n**iLISI:** 0.950\n**cLISI:** 0.971\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.327\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.659  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.674  NMI: 0.693\n  Graph_conn: 0.996  kBET: 0.791  iLISI: 0.950  cLISI: 0.971\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.327\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.830496  ASW_label: 0.555112  ARI: 0.674345  NMI: 0.693309\n  Graph_conn: 0.995690  kBET: 0.754598  iLISI: 0.949657  cLISI: 0.991515\n  PCR: 0.999979  Cell_cycle: 0.287468\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1019\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission and it now runs without crashing.\n\
    \n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two fundamental errors:\n\n1. **Incorrect function name**: Called `mpb.embed_graphfwpca()` which doesn't exist. The actual function is `mpb.eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca()`.\n\n2. **Non-existent helper functions**: The code attempted to call:\n   - `brbg.brbg_balance()` - This function does not exist in the `brbg_common` module\n   - `daqb.apply_daqb()` - This function does not exist in the `bbsg_density_adaptive` module\n\n   The agent appeared to be trying to implement a multi-stage pipeline by manually applying BRBG and DAQB on top of the MPB-GraphFWPCA results. However, the `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca()` function already includes the full pipeline internally (normalization, HVG selection, GraphFWPCA embedding, BRBG balancing, and DAQB).\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nCreated `submission_v3.py` that correctly uses the MPB-GraphFWPCA pipeline:\n\n1. **Corrected function call**: Changed from `embed_graphfwpca` to `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca`\n\n2. **Simplified\
    \ approach**: Instead of trying to manually apply BRBG and DAQB (which have different interfaces than expected), used the complete integrated pipeline that `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca` provides\n\n3. **Preserved agent's intent**: Configured the function with parameters matching the agent's goals from the submission title:\n   - `n_pcs_graph=100` - High PCA dimensions for graph construction\n   - `k_total=50` - 50 nearest neighbors (as mentioned in title: \"k=50\")\n   - `kdensity=22` - Density parameter (as mentioned in title: \"kd=22\")\n   - `delta=0.10` - Delta parameter for density adaptation\n\nThe fix recognizes that the `eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca` function is a complete end-to-end pipeline that already incorporates all the techniques the agent was trying to apply manually (MPB normalization, GraphFWPCA embedding, BRBG balancing, and DAQB).\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script confirmed the code runs successfully for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The evaluation is\
    \ processing normally, just taking time to complete\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys, numpy as np, scipy.sparse as sp\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\n\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nimport mpb_graphfwpca_override as mpb\n\ndef _ensure_csr(m):\n    return m.tocsr() if hasattr(m, \"tocsr\") else sp.csr_matrix(m)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # The eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca function already does the full pipeline:\n    # - Normalization\n    # - HVG selection\n    # - GraphFWPCA embedding\n    # - BRBG balancing with fixed lambda\n    # - DAQB (density-adaptive balanced graph)\n    # It returns an adata with connectivities and distances already set\n\n    # Use the complete pipeline with customized parameters\n    # n_pcs_graph=100 (agent wanted high\
    \ PCA dims for graph)\n    # k_total=50 (agent mentioned k=50 in title)\n    # kdensity=22 (agent mentioned kd=22 in title)\n    # Other parameters use the defaults from the function\n    adata = mpb.eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        n_pcs_graph=100,\n        k_total=50,\n        kdensity=22,\n        delta=0.10,\n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/9c520cde-f5a0-4aa6-8448-0c3456cc0371/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 9c520cde-f5a0-4aa6-8448-0c3456cc0371\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally\
    \ and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Masked-weights (row-normalized) using DAQB mask from MPB‑GraphFWPCA (k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1020.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title\
