parts:
- text: "Weighted-connectivity underperforms; ending the line and prepping the addendum for Archive next tick.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 45}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 661): Weighted-connectivity results finalized.\n  - Masked weights v1 (ID 1019): 0.7309 (auto-debug rerouted to lam=0.70; not the intended test). Metrics [ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle] =\n    [0.659, 0.248, 0.674, 0.693, 0.996, 0.791, 0.950, 0.971, 1.000, 0.327].\n  - Masked weights v2 row-normalized (ID 1020): 0.6626 (true masked-weights using DAQB mask + EtC weights). Metrics =\n    [0.659, 0.248, 0.626, 0.722, 0.913, 0.789, 0.352, 0.990, 1.000, 0.327].\n  - Auto‑k (ID 1011): 0.7396 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.760, 0.713, 0.967, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.327].\n  - Auto‑kd (ID 1013): 0.7373 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.758, 0.714, 0.967, 0.788, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.305].\n  - SOTA ref (ID 960): 0.7465 → [0.659, 0.248, 0.774, 0.728, 0.968, 0.789, 0.961, 0.973, 1.000, 0.366].\n\
    \n  Conclusion\n  - Restoring weights on the DAQB-selected edge set does not help; it harms mixing (iLISI collapse to 0.3516 raw; normalized 0.352) and reduces ARI/NMI.\n  - Binary connectivities with true distances remain preferred under the fixed SOTA config (k=50,kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10, cap=2.0).\n  - Graph Health auto-selection is insufficient near the ridge; minor gains/losses hinge on label metrics outside GHS’s scope.\n\n  Action\n  - End weighting/auto‑k,kd line. Next tick (cooldown expiry), submit Archive addendum from this capsule via source_private with spec‑ordered vectors for 1011, 1013, 1019 (noted), and 1020.\n```"
