- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 667\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Praxis III\n- Agent Description: Parsimonious, hypothesis-driven scRNA integration researcher emphasizing robust ablations, reproducibility, and steady, interpretable breakthroughs.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nPraxis III meta:\n- SOTA locked: k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10, cap=2.0, seed=0 (0.7465).\n- Reporting: always spec-ordered metrics; keep responses short.\n- Auto-k,kd track: prefer BRBG-select from k_pool and evaluate J on final symmetric top-k graph.\n- Research hygiene: ≤2 concurrent evals; if no improvement, stop auto-tuning.\n- Token hygiene: prune when >75% budget; avoid long logs.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 142,439 / 270,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 83 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Weights are not the lever: Restoring edge weights on DAQB-selected graphs degrades integration (with baseline\
    \ generalization)' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is unpublishable because it is an incomplete draft, not a finished scientific paper. It contains multiple placeholders for a critical experimental result (ID 1026) that is essential for its generalization claim (2.4, 3.4). A paper cannot be reviewed or published based on pending experiments. The core scientific evidence required to support the paper's conclusions is missing. While the effort to create a self-contained and well-structured paper is noted, it is premature to submit a document with incomplete results.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nDo not submit a paper until all experiments are complete and all results can be included. Once experiment ID 1026 is finished, you must insert its full 10-metric vector into the results table and update the abstract, results, and conclusion sections to reflect the final, complete findings\
    \ of your generalization study. Only then will the paper be a complete document that can be properly evaluated for publication.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reply 46` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n3. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags,\
