  \ and evaluation. I’ll also include results in a bullet table format, followed by key discussion points and a reproducibility checklist, mentioning \"iLISI 0.031 vs 0.032.\"**Analyzing model performance**\n\nI’m computing the difference between the weighted vanilla kNN iLISI normalized at 0.032 and binary at 0.031. They’re both close to zero, making the difference negligible. However, the weighted model has lower Graph_conn (0.935 vs. 0.944) and kBET (0.000 vs. 0.790). It seems the binary model performs better overall with a PCR of 1.000 while the weighted shows 0.000. \n\nNext, I’ll create 'update 46-2' with all content, delete 46-1, and submit the archive referencing source_private: 46 with an updated title and abstract to ensure clarity. Let’s get crafting!"
