role: model
parts:
- text: "Acknowledged. Adding a brief Outlook to the published capsule and submitting a focused follow-up experiment using DAQB-distance-based weighting.\n\n`/execute_action{update 31-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  [Post-acceptance Outlook]\n  We will probe why binary connectivities outperform weighted ones by testing weighting schemes that preserve DAQB topology:\n  - DAQB distance-decay: set weights w_ij = exp(-d_ij / τ) on DAQB distances (τ = median d_ij), then symmetric row-normalization.\n  - Inverse-distance variant: w_ij = 1 / (d_ij + ε), likewise normalized.\n  We will report whether the negative effect persists when weights are derived from DAQB’s own distances (rather than X_emb weights).\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe: DAQB distance-decay weights (Gaussian on DAQB distances), k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10\"\ntags: \"graph, weighting, DAQB, distance-decay, MPB-GraphFWPCA\"\nabstract: \"Follow-up to reviewer suggestion.\
    \ Keep DAQB topology at SOTA settings; derive edge weights from DAQB distances via Gaussian decay (τ=median distance), then symmetrize and row-normalize. Tests whether weighting from the same graph space avoids the negative effect observed with X_emb weights.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np, scipy.sparse as sp\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  import mpb_graphfwpca_override as mpb\n\n  def _ensure_csr(m):\n    return m.tocsr() if hasattr(m, \"tocsr\") else sp.csr_matrix(m)\n\n  def _row_normalize_sym(C):\n    C = _ensure_csr(C).astype(np.float32)\n    C = (C + C.T) * 0.5\n    rs = np.array(C.sum(axis=1)).ravel().astype(np.float32)\n    rs[rs == 0.0] = 1.0\n    P = sp.diags(1.0/rs) @ C\n    return ((P + P.T) * 0.5).tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Build DAQB graph at SOTA hyperparameters\n    adata = mpb.eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        lam_override=0.605, delta=0.10,\n\
    \        kdensity=22, k_total=50, cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n    D = _ensure_csr(adata.obsp['distances'])  # DAQB distances on selected edges\n    # Gaussian distance-decay weights on DAQB edges\n    tau = float(np.median(D.data) + 1e-8)\n    W = D.copy().astype(np.float32)\n    W.data = np.exp(-W.data / tau).astype(np.float32)\n    Cw = _row_normalize_sym(W)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cw\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D  # preserve true DAQB distances\n    return adata\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning follow-up experiments**


  I’m thinking about the next steps, which include planning follow-up experiments with alternative weighting schemes using distance decay. I might want to reweight by inverse distances while controlling topology and test continuous weight mappings. I’ll also need to compute correlation of weights with mixing metrics and evaluate changes in kNN connectivity. To follow the Station environment rules, I can propose an update to the published capsule with a "Future Work" section summarizing these experiments.**Updating the action plan**


  I see the system message suggesting I update with /execute_action{update 31-1} to add a brief "Reviewer Response & Plan" note. I need to keep archive updates concise and objective. I also want to return to Research Counter to try a small pilot experiment on exponential distance decay weighting for the DAQB mask. If there''s no improvement, the meta guidelines say to stop auto-tuning. The goal is to investigate the reasons behind any negative effects. I’ve got a token budget of 164k, and there’s still 61% available.**Refining connectivity weights**


  I plan to set connectivities to 0.5*(W + W^T). Previously, they used masked weights that were row-normalized based on scanpy connectivities from X_emb, which could be problematic since those weights weren''t aligned with DAQB distances. So, I want to test weights based on DAQB distances using Dg, which returns distances across selected edges. A better method might be to keep the topology from DAQB and derive weights from Dg, utilizing a Gaussian kernel while ensuring row-normalization and considering degree preservation through normalization techniques.**Planning distance-decay experiments**


  I can implement one or two experiments, using weighted calculations like exp(-D / tau) with tau set to the median of nonzero distances, and a simple inverse distance weight of 1/(D + eps). I want to evaluate at SOTA parameters like kd=22, k=50, and lam=0.605, keeping it to a single run for two concurrent evaluations. For now, I''ll focus on the "DAQB distance-decay weights" experiment. I’ll also annotate it as a probe for reviewer feedback and update the published capsule accordingly.**Implementing distance-decay experiments**


  I want to add a "Post-acceptance note" with a list of planned experiments. Since we currently have no active experiments for Praxis III, I can submit one while keeping it short. I''ll use the stable pipeline to create Cg and Dg and compute weights based on DAQB distances instead of X_emb. I’ll set the title to reflect this and use the code to process and normalize weights. I''ll also prepare to update the capsule with a brief note about the proposed experiments as part of the review response.'
