parts:
- text: "Queuing one more follow-up: inverse-distance weights on DAQB distances (stay within ≤2 concurrent evals).\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Probe: DAQB inverse-distance weights on DAQB distances, k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ=0.10\"\ntags: \"graph, weighting, DAQB, inverse-distance, MPB-GraphFWPCA\"\nabstract: \"Follow-up probe. Keep DAQB topology at SOTA; set weights w_ij = 1/(d_ij+ε) from DAQB distances, then symmetrize and row-normalize. Tests if DAQB-native weights avoid the negative effect seen with X_emb-derived weights.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, numpy as np, scipy.sparse as sp\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  import mpb_graphfwpca_override as mpb\n\n  def _ensure_csr(m):\n    return m.tocsr() if hasattr(m, \"tocsr\") else sp.csr_matrix(m)\n\n  def _row_normalize_sym(C):\n    C = _ensure_csr(C).astype(np.float32)\n    C = (C + C.T) * 0.5\n    rs = np.array(C.sum(axis=1)).ravel().astype(np.float32)\n    rs[rs == 0.0] = 1.0\n   \
    \ P = sp.diags(1.0/rs) @ C\n    return ((P + P.T) * 0.5).tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Build DAQB graph at SOTA hyperparameters\n    adata = mpb.eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca(\n        adata,\n        lam_override=0.605, delta=0.10,\n        kdensity=22, k_total=50, cap=2.0,\n        rng_seed=0\n    )\n    D = _ensure_csr(adata.obsp['distances'])  # DAQB distances on selected edges\n\n    # Inverse-distance weights on DAQB edges with gentle clipping\n    eps = 1e-6\n    inv = 1.0 / (D.data.astype(np.float32) + eps)\n    # Clip extreme weights to 99.5th percentile to avoid numerical dominance\n    hi = np.percentile(inv, 99.5)\n    inv = np.minimum(inv, hi).astype(np.float32)\n\n    W = D.copy().astype(np.float32)\n    W.data = inv\n\n    Cw = _row_normalize_sym(W)\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cw\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D  # preserve true DAQB distances\n    return adata\n```"
thinking_content: '**Planning experiments and research hygiene**


  I need to respond to the user''s last message. It seems the follow-up probe experiment 1035 is running successfully, and the archive update to add Outlook succeeded. As Praxis III, I''m focused on research hygiene, which allows ≤2 concurrent evaluations, and right now, we have one running. I can queue a second experiment on inverse-distance weighting to test a reviewer suggestion. Our token usage is at 62%, so I’ll go ahead and submit the second experiment.**Preparing for submission and tracking**


  I want to include a clipped exponent base to prevent high weights at small distances, adding a minimum cap for that. After the results, I''ll prepare a short addendum for Capsule #31 with the findings, but I won’t update it until I have the results. I could make a quick note in Private memory to track this plan, but it’s not essential. So, I’ll set up the commands for submission and produce the appropriate YAML content. I’ll make sure the code aligns with the interface requirements.**Ensuring proper weight application**


  I need to ensure the weights are applied only to existing edges, confirming D is the distances matrix of the DAQB graph. I’ll row-normalize symmetrically, just like in function 1035. I should consider that distances could be zero for identical points, but self-distances will be removed. To avoid heavy tails, I’ll add epsilon (1e-6) and cap quantiles. I’ll propose the submission with the title "Probe: DAQB inverse-distance weights" and update the abstract to match previous submissions. Let''s write the code to implement W as 1 / (D.data + eps).**Refining the weight distribution**


