role: model
parts:
- text: "1035 result: 0.6809. DAQB-native Gaussian weights improve over X_emb weights (iLISI 0.409 vs 0.352; ARI/NMI up) but remain below SOTA 0.7465 and hurt cLISI vs SOTA. Awaiting 1037; will append both probes to Capsule #31.\n\nPruning large earlier ticks to conserve tokens.\n\n`/execute_action{goto token_management}`\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"660\"\n    summary: \"Submitted masked-weights (row-normalized) using DAQB mask over MPB‑GraphFWPCA (EID 1020). Result 0.6626 with vector; planned to end weighting line if <0.742 and prepared addendum draft (#45).\"\n  - ticks: \"659\"\n    summary: \"Received auto-debug note for masked-weights v1 (EID 1019=0.7309; not the intended masked test). Submitted corrected masked-weights v2 (EID 1020) using DAQB mask + EtC weights with row-normalization.\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing model performance**\n\nI’m planning to give a quick analysis of my findings. The 1035 results improved over 1020, but they’re still below the state-of-the-art (SOTA). The iLISI improved from 0.352 to 0.409, and ARI/NMI showed stronger improvements. However, cLISI decreased to 0.869, which suggests more mixing is harming the cell type structure. Lower cLISI means worse label preservation. It seems that changes to the weights dampen iLISI degradation but negatively impact cLISI. Balancing this is still below SOTA, but the masked weights v2 are better than SOTA.**Planning updates and token management**\n\nI noticed that the weighted decays have brought cLISI down to 0.869, which is ironically below SOTA. I'm deciding to wait for the results from 1037 before drafting an addendum update for Archive capsule 31 to include the new data. We only have 1037 currently running and 1035 finished, so we can't schedule more evaluations. In the meantime, I’ll prune tokens and\
  \ potentially update the \"Outlook\" list in Private Memory. I'll prune the tokens with lengths over a certain threshold and list the necessary information for that process.**Summarizing tick actions**\n\nI need to add a summary for the ticks. For tick 660, we submitted the 1020 masked row normalized weights with a score of 0.6626 and created a negative results plan. This tick also included the evaluation that led to capsule #45. \n\nFor tick 659, I submitted the 1020 and received a 1019 result of 0.7309. It’s important to make sure the tick numbers align properly, as 1019 was queued at 658. It looks like we should prune 660 and 659 due to their larger sizes.**Implementing pruning actions**\n\nI’m noticing that there's a cooldown for performing a prune every X ticks, and since I pruned at 663, I can proceed now at 670, which is great. So, I'll go to token management and initiate a prune response for ticks 660 and 659.\n\nFor tick 660, the summary is that we submitted masked weights using\
  \ the DAQB mask with a result of 0.6626 and drafted addendum #45. For tick 659, I received an auto-debug note for a different version and submitted the corrected weights. I’m considering pruning tick 668 as well but will hold off on that for now. I'll also focus on drafting the planned append to the paper later.**Planning actions and interpretations**\n\nI’m ready to implement a few actions here. First, I'll provide a quick interpretation: 1035 has shown improvement, but the weighting from DAQB distances still causes some harm, keeping the results below SOTA. We're waiting for 1037 to arrive.\n\nNext, I'll carry out the prune actions, and importantly, I plan to append the results to the capsule once 1037 is evaluated. I’ll also remember to use YAML quoting for any special characters when crafting the response. Let’s proceed!"
